WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.634
-Adam, welcome, welcome

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.367
-Thanks, man.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.067
-to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:03.868
Thanks for coming on.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.234
It's great to see you.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:06.400
I heard that

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.634
you actually just came back
from Italy.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:12.634
-Yeah, like just
right before I came here.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:17.934
We were in Tuscany for a wedding
that Dakota Johnson was not at.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.133
-Oh, yeah, she should've
showed up at that.

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.234
-It wasn't the one

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:23.467
-It wasn't the one.
-that she crashed.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:25.667
-She picks one a year
that she crashes, yeah.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.234
[ Laughter ]
Once in a lifetime,

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:29.334
she'll crash a wedding.
-One lucky couple every year.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:30.834
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. It wasn't that one.

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.434
Oh, Tuscany must've
been beautiful.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:34.267
-Yeah, yeah, it's beautiful.
-I've never been there.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.634
I want to go.
-Oh, really?

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.868
We went to Florence and we go --

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:41.300
Whenever we go
to any foreign country,

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.567
my wife, Naomi,
she's really good about --

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.767
She's one of those people that
like brushes up on the language

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.834
and is like essentially fluent
-Wow.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:50.534
-by the time we get there.
-Oh, cool.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:53.000
-Which is great
because everyone like comments

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.634
on how good she is
and she gets us around.

00:00:55.634 --> 00:01:00.300
But also, I'm just such --
I'm such an idiot

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.734
[ Laughter ]
because I don't --
I don't know anything.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:06.000
Like I don't know --
I struggle like saying --

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.300
I don't even know a word.
-One word.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.267
-No.
-No.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:12.033
And so I always like find myself

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:16.467
and it's so lame
and so embarrassing,

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.534
but I always --
I always end up like --

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:21.467
like saying English words
with like a terrible --

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:24.934
like an approximation
of an accent.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:29.334
[ Laughter ]
Like the other day,
I really find myself saying,

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:31.367
[ Changing accent ]
Uh, yes, uh.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:33.434
Do you -- Do you have a, uh,

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:34.767
a phone charger?

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.300
Yes, um.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.634
Yes, please."
And the guy's like,

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:43.334
"Do you need a phone charger?
I can just get you

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:45.033
[ Laughter ]
a phone charger."
-You're the one with the for--

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.801
[ Changes accent ]
How you say --

00:01:46.801 --> 00:01:48.267
[ Changes accent ]
How do you say phone?

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:51.434
Grazie, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:53.100
-That's so funny.
-Oh, it's so bad.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.234
-We were talking backstage
and we were talking

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:56.834
about you said that you met one

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:59.167
of your favorite actors
of all time,

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:01.234
the great Al Pacino.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:02.667
-I've never gotten to meet

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.200
Al Pacino.
-You haven't met Al Pacino?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.634
-No, but I love Al Pacino.
-Oh, my God.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:10.200
-He's one of my faves as well.
-Yeah. He's like my very

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.534
fave -- You know, actors,
you know, it's Al Pacino.

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:15.100
-That's your guy.
-Yeah, he's my guy

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.501
and he's kind of the guy

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:19.868
and we were at the
Vanity Fair Oscar party,

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:22.467
which is like all famous --
Like it's the place you go

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.200
if you want to feel less famous

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.767
[ Laughter ]
because they're all there.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.133
-Everyone's there.
-[Both] Yeah.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.601
-And I was talking
to Kevin Bacon,

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.834
which is also very cool,
and he was like,

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:35.601
"Hey, I was just talking
to Al Pacino."

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:38.701
And I was like, "Oh!
Al Pacino's here?"

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:40.234
He's like,
"Yeah, he's right over there.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:42.868
You should go check it out.
Check out Al Pacino."

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:45.234
[ Laughter ]
That's my guy!
-That's your dude.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:47.234
-And so I grabbed Naomi,
I grabbed my wife,

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:49.501
and I'm like,
"Let's go look at Al Pacino."

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.234
[ Laughter ]
I don't want to like talk
to him.

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.167
-No, of course not.
-No. What would I say?

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:55.767
-It's like the Mona Lisa.
-Right.

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.067
[ Laughter ]
-You just want to go look at it.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:59.000
-Take a gander.
-Take a gander at Al Pacino.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.734
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. So, she's like,
"Oh, come on."

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:05.334
So we go over and I find
this spot like 15 yards.

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:06.634
[ Laughter ]
Sure enough, he's right there.

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:09.267
He's on like this couch
with a bunch of people.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:12.334
And I find us spots like
under a potted palm tree,

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:15.100
[ Laughter ]
so we're kind of hidden

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.968
and I'm just like, "Let's just
look at him for five minutes

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:19.968
and then we can go."
-Get outta here, yeah.

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:22.901
-And so we're there and I'm
like, "It's him. He's there."

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:25.267
And I see him.
I kind of glance. I'm like,

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:27.901
"Yeah, he's there." There he is
and he's talking to people.

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:31.133
Take another look over.
He's still there. It's awesome.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.501
And then it was like
the third time I looked,

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.133
it was like a horror movie
or something because,

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:38.367
the third time I look,
he's just looking right at me.

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:39.634
[ Laughter ]
It's like, "Oh!"

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:41.868
And not only is he looking
at me,

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:44.634
he like looks at me
and then he starts getting up

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:50.501
and walks over like one of those
ottoman/foot rest things,

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:51.434
this giant thing.

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:52.968
And he's like climbing over it,

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:55.467
[ Laughter ]
coming straight at us.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.934
And I'm like, "Al Pacino.
He's coming.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:04:00.901
He's coming. Al Pacino is like
walking over to us."

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.100
-Yeah.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.934
-Sure enough, he comes right up
and he's like --

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:08.300
I can't --
I don't really do a Pacino.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.367
You do, right?
-I could try, sure.

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:12.300
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, okay. He goes --

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:16.367
[ As Pacino ]
Oh, I -- I-I love your show.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:19.501
So.
-[ As Pacino ] I love your show!

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:20.601
-Yes!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:22.400
[ Cheering and applause ]
I love Sev--

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.200
"Severance"?
-"Severance."
"I love 'Severance.'"

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.100
-"I love 'Severance'"?
Al Pacino said that to you?

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.100
-He said, "I love 'Severance'

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.400
and my son and I watch it
together."

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.868
Yeah, I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:32.968
-What you did say back to him?

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:34.567
-I was like, "You have no idea.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.734
I was here --
I just wanted to look at you.

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.567
[ Laughter and applause ]
And --"

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.701
-This is a bonus.

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.100
-I was like,
he'll never believe me,

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.567
but, "That's what I was doing
here, was looking at you."

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:48.334
And I'm like, "Because you're
my guy, you're the best one."

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.934
[ Laughter ]
-Wow!
-You're my favorite?

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:50.734
[ Cheering and applause ]
-You got to say that to him?

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:51.801
-Yeah, I said it to him.

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:54.100
-Good for you.
-Yeah.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.634
-Brought a photo, which I asked.

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:58.667
Here's a photo of you
and Al Pacino right there.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:04:59.934
-Yeah.
-The one and only.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:02.200
-That's the moment, right there.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
-He asked me for a photo.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.767
It was crazy.
-How cool is that?

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:08.200
-It was pretty cool.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.367
-Everyone loves "Severance,"
by the way. Congrats.

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:12.868
The reviews,
rave reviews on the show.
-Oh, thank you.

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:16.834
-We had Ben Stiller on the show
for "Severance" when it first --

00:05:16.834 --> 00:05:18.767
He directed a few episodes.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.501
-You crush it in this show.
It's so good.

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:22.100
-Thanks. Thank you.
-Congrats on the success of it.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.834
It just got picked up
for Season 2.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.934
[ Cheering and applause ]
Thank you.

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:29.534
-It's so --
It's such a great idea

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:32.067
and it's so well-executed.
Congrats on that.

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:33.300
-Thanks.
-Can you describe --

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.901
How do you describe the show
to people?

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.434
-It's weird.

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:41.934
It's like it's sort of
a workplace thriller

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:44.667
sort of comedy,
where it takes place in a world

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:49.167
where Lumon Industries is this
company who has this technology.

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:51.501
Insert a microchip
into your brain, so,

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:55.100
when you cross the threshold
at your work, at your job,

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.000
suddenly, you don't know who you
are in the outside world.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.868
It separates your memories
so all you know is work.

00:06:01.868 --> 00:06:04.100
And then when you leave work
at the end of the day,

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.901
it deactivates the chip,
so you have no memory

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:09.367
of who you are at work
or what you did there.

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:12.634
So it just completely separates
your two realities,

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:13.934
work and life.

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:16.801
-Yeah. And it's so well done.
It's so well shot

00:06:16.801 --> 00:06:18.934
and it gets tricky
and you're fantastic in it.

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:20.801
-Thanks, man.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:23.434
Here's Adam Scott
in "Severance." Take a look.

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:25.434
-Clearly, he was trying
to tell you something.

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:27.167
-Uh, no.

00:06:27.167 --> 00:06:28.567
-Go lick a boob, Mark.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:32.934
You're more loyal to this place
than to your friend.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:35.367
-I'm loyal to how it felt
around here

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:36.801
before you showed up.

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:38.167
-You mean when Petey was here?

00:06:38.167 --> 00:06:40.300
-Yeah, because there
was balance.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.567
We could have fun and work

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:45.067
without the whole
[bleep] department imploding.

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:46.400
-Work is [bleep].

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:50.200
-The work is mysterious
and important

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.901
and we deal with the uncertainty
it brings us

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:56.434
in the way that Kier
would've wanted --

00:06:56.434 --> 00:06:59.067
together, as a family.

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:02.367
-I could not,

00:07:02.367 --> 00:07:04.834
with a razor to my throat,

00:07:04.834 --> 00:07:07.000
be less interested
in being your family.

00:07:08.067 --> 00:07:09.934
-Oh!
Come on!

00:07:09.934 --> 00:07:11.501
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:07:11.501 --> 00:07:13.100
Adam Scott, everybody!

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.667
"Severance" is streaming now
on Apple TV+.

00:07:16.667 --> 00:07:19.267
Carrie Underwood performs
after the break.

00:07:19.267 --> 00:07:20.300
Stick around, everybody.

